    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d272">

                <pb facs="0375" n="209" sameAs="frus:frus1917/pg209"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 893. 811/243</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        Ambassador Guthrie
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1917-01-22T16:00:00-05:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">January 22, 1917, 4 p.m</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Your telegram of January 18, 3 p.m. For your information. Japanese Government is
                    pressing the American International Corporation for an interest in the contract
                    for the improvement of the Grand Canal in China. China unwilling but Corporation
                    hopes may consent to issue of part of bonds at Tokyo with Americans retaining
                    entire management.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Lansing</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
